              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Morgan Madsen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The only thing I did differently was to use a box carrot cake mix instead of a spice cake mix. Otherwise I followed the recipe exactly and it turned out perfectly. Next time I think I'd try adding a little coconut."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "deniseg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I remember this well from my childhood in the 60’s&amp;70’s. mom made it for Easter dinner dessert. It’s not hard to make. You can bake in a 9x13” pan, cool, then top with cream cheese frosting instead of lemon juice &amp; powdered sugar. It’s delicious either way. In autumn, I substitute a 15 oz can lof plain pumpkin puree instead of the tomato soup. Pumpkin spice cake is very tasty too. Cupcakes from this recipe make a great contribution to a children’s Halloween party at school.",
            "datePublished": "2025-04-17T15:19:07.219Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
